{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/definition-classification/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/definition-classification.html","area":"students","kind":"topic","title":"Definition & Classification of Matter | Chemistry Foundations","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <!-- Navigation -->\n    <nav class=\"mb-4 flex items-center justify-between\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/foundations/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-800 transition flex items-center\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Foundations\n      </a>\n      <div class=\"flex items-center gap-3\">\n        <div class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">\n          <span id=\"topic-progress-text\" data-bidemy=\"progress-text\">0% Complete</span>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"w-24 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded-full overflow-hidden\" data-bidemy=\"progress\">\n          <div id=\"topic-progress-bar\" class=\"h-full bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-400 to-green-500 transition-all duration-300\" style=\"width: 0%\"></div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -flask text-emerald-500 mr-3\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Definition &amp; Classification of Matter\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding what chemistry is and how matter is classified into elements, compounds, and mixtures.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-emerald-50 border-l-4 border-emerald-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-emerald-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-emerald-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Define chemistry and matter</li>\n          <li>• Distinguish between elements, compounds, and mixtures</li>\n          <li>• Classify substances as elements, compounds, or mixtures</li>\n          <li>• Differentiate between homogeneous and heterogeneous mixtures</li>\n          <li>• Understand the difference between metals and non-metals</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: What is Chemistry? -->\n      <section id=\"section-1\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          What is Chemistry?\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-100 to-green-100 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4 text-center\">\n            <p class=\"text-2xl font-bold text-emerald-700 mb-2\">Chemistry</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">is the scientific study of the composition, structure, properties, and changes of matter.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-emerald-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -atom mr-2\" data-mi=\"atom\">atom</span>Matter</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Anything that has mass and occupies space. Examples: air, water, rocks, plants, metals.</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-emerald-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -cogs mr-2\" data-mi=\"settings\">settings</span>Energy</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">The capacity to do work. Chemistry also studies energy changes during reactions (heat, light, etc.).</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n          <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Branches of Chemistry</h4>\n          <div class=\"grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-2 text-sm\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\"><strong>Physical</strong><br><span class=\"text-xs\">Energy &amp; reactions</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\"><strong>Organic</strong><br><span class=\"text-xs\">Carbon compounds</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\"><strong>Inorganic</strong><br><span class=\"text-xs\">Non-carbon</span></div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-2 rounded text-center\"><strong>Analytical</strong><br><span class=\"text-xs\">Testing &amp; analysis</span></div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Classification of Matter -->\n      <section id=\"section-2\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Classification of Matter\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Matter can be classified based on its composition. The main categories are:</p>\n\n          <!-- Classification Diagram -->\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"text-center mb-4\">\n              <div class=\"inline-block bg-emerald-600 text-white px-6 py-2 rounded-lg font-bold\">MATTER</div>\n              <div class=\"flex justify-center mt-2\">\n                <div class=\"w-0.5 h-6 bg-gray-400\"></div>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"flex justify-center gap-8 md:gap-16\">\n                <div>\n                  <div class=\"w-0.5 h-4 bg-gray-400 mx-auto\"></div>\n                  <div class=\"bg-blue-500 text-white px-4 py-1 rounded font-medium text-sm\">Pure Substances</div>\n                  <div class=\"flex justify-center gap-4 mt-2\">\n                    <div>\n                      <div class=\"w-0.5 h-3 bg-gray-400 mx-auto\"></div>\n                      <div class=\"bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 px-3 py-1 rounded text-xs\">Elements</div>\n                    </div>\n                    <div>\n                      <div class=\"w-0.5 h-3 bg-gray-400 mx-auto\"></div>\n                      <div class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-800 px-3 py-1 rounded text-xs\">Compounds</div>\n                    </div>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n                <div>\n                  <div class=\"w-0.5 h-4 bg-gray-400 mx-auto\"></div>\n                  <div class=\"bg-orange-500 text-white px-4 py-1 rounded font-medium text-sm\">Mixtures</div>\n                  <div class=\"flex justify-center gap-4 mt-2\">\n                    <div>\n                      <div class=\"w-0.5 h-3 bg-gray-400 mx-auto\"></div>\n                      <div class=\"bg-orange-100 text-orange-800 px-3 py-1 rounded text-xs\">Homogeneous</div>\n                    </div>\n                    <div>\n                      <div class=\"w-0.5 h-3 bg-gray-400 mx-auto\"></div>\n                      <div class=\"bg-red-100 text-red-800 px-3 py-1 rounded text-xs\">Heterogeneous</div>\n                    </div>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: Elements -->\n      <section id=\"section-3\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          Elements\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-50 to-indigo-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-1\">Definition</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">An <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">element</strong> is a pure substance that cannot be broken down into simpler substances by chemical means. It consists of only one type of atom.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -cube mr-2\" data-mi=\"view_in_ar\">view_in_ar</span>Metals</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Shiny (lustrous)</li>\n                <li>• Good conductors of heat &amp; electricity</li>\n                <li>• Malleable (can be hammered)</li>\n                <li>• Ductile (can be drawn into wires)</li>\n                <li>• High melting points</li>\n              </ul>\n              <p class=\"text-blue-600 text-sm mt-2\"><strong>Examples:</strong> Iron, Copper, Gold, Sodium</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -cube mr-2\" data-mi=\"view_in_ar\">view_in_ar</span>Non-Metals</h4>\n              <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n                <li>• Dull (non-lustrous)</li>\n                <li>• Poor conductors</li>\n                <li>• Brittle (break easily)</li>\n                <li>• Low melting points</li>\n                <li>• Can be solids, liquids, or gases</li>\n              </ul>\n              <p class=\"text-purple-600 text-sm mt-2\"><strong>Examples:</strong> Carbon, Oxygen, Chlorine, Sulfur</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-green-50 p-3 rounded-lg border border-green-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-green-800 mb-1\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-1\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Metalloids</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Elements with properties between metals and non-metals. Examples: Silicon, Germanium, Boron. Used in electronics (semiconductors).</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Compounds -->\n      <section id=\"section-4\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Compounds\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-50 to-pink-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-1\">Definition</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A <strong class=\"text-purple-600\">compound</strong> is a pure substance formed when two or more elements combine chemically in fixed proportions.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 mb-4\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3\">Key Characteristics of Compounds:</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span class=\"mi -check text-green-500 mt-1\" data-mi=\"check\">check</span> Elements combine in <strong>fixed ratios</strong> by mass</li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span class=\"mi -check text-green-500 mt-1\" data-mi=\"check\">check</span> Properties are <strong>different</strong> from constituent elements</li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span class=\"mi -check text-green-500 mt-1\" data-mi=\"check\">check</span> Can only be separated by <strong>chemical means</strong></li>\n              <li class=\"flex items-start gap-2\"><span class=\"mi -check text-green-500 mt-1\" data-mi=\"check\">check</span> Components are chemically <strong>bonded</strong></li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 border-l-4 border-yellow-400 p-4 rounded-r-lg\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-yellow-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Example: Water (H₂O)</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm\">Hydrogen (flammable gas) + Oxygen (supports burning) → Water (extinguishes fire)</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-600 text-sm mt-1\">The properties of water are completely different from hydrogen and oxygen!</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Example -->\n        <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n          <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n            <span><span class=\"mi -calculator mr-2 text-purple-500\" data-mi=\"calculate\">calculate</span>Worked Example: Identifying Compounds</span>\n            <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n          </button>\n          <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n            <div class=\"p-5\">\n              <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Classify the following as elements or compounds: H₂O, O₂, NaCl, Fe, CO₂, N₂</p>\n\n              <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-blue-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-blue-500\">\n                  <p class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800\">Elements</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm\">O₂, Fe, N₂ - contain only one type of atom</p>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"step-card bg-purple-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                  <p class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800\">Compounds</p>\n                  <p class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm\">H₂O, NaCl, CO₂ - contain two or more different atoms chemically combined</p>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Mixtures -->\n      <section id=\"section-5\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Mixtures\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-orange-50 to-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg mb-4 border-l-4 border-orange-500\">\n            <p class=\"text-lg font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-1\">Definition</p>\n            <p class=\"text-gray-700\">A <strong class=\"text-orange-600\">mixture</strong> consists of two or more substances physically combined. The components can be present in any proportion and can be separated by physical means.</p>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-orange-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-orange-800 mb-2\">Homogeneous Mixtures</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">Uniform throughout - cannot see individual components</p>\n              <p class=\"text-orange-600 text-sm\"><strong>Examples:</strong> Salt solution, air, alloys (bronze, steel), soft drinks</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">Also called \"solutions\"</p>\n            </div>\n            <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n              <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-red-800 mb-2\">Heterogeneous Mixtures</h4>\n              <p class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm mb-2\">Non-uniform - can see different components</p>\n              <p class=\"text-red-600 text-sm\"><strong>Examples:</strong> Sand and water, oil and water, salad, rocks</p>\n              <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2\">Components are visibly distinct</p>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Key Differences from Compounds:</h4>\n            <ul class=\"text-gray-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n              <li>• Components can be in <strong>any proportion</strong></li>\n              <li>• Can be separated by <strong>physical means</strong> (filtration, distillation, etc.)</li>\n              <li>• Properties are a <strong>combination</strong> of the components</li>\n              <li>• No <strong>chemical bonds</strong> between components</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 6: Comparison Table -->\n      <section id=\"section-6\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-emerald-100 text-emerald-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">6</span>\n          Summary: Elements, Compounds &amp; Mixtures\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm border-collapse border border-gray-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <thead class=\"bg-emerald-600 text-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-left\">Property</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Element</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Compound</th>\n                <th class=\"border border-gray-300 p-3 text-center\">Mixture</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Composition</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">One type of atom</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Two or more elements chemically combined</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Two or more substances physically combined</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Proportion</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">N/A</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Fixed ratio</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Variable ratio</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Separation</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Cannot be separated</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Chemical means only</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Physical means</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-gray-50\">\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Properties</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Unique to element</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Different from constituents</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Same as constituents</td>\n              </tr>\n              <tr>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 font-medium\">Examples</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">O₂, Fe, Cu, C</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">H₂O, NaCl, CO₂</td>\n                <td class=\"border border-gray-300 p-2 text-center\">Air, salt solution, sand+water</td>\n              </tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 7: Practice Problems -->\n      <section id=\"section-7\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-emerald-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Classify each as element, compound, or mixture: (a) Air, (b) Gold, (c) Carbon dioxide, (d) Salt solution</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700 space-y-1\">\n                <p>(a) Air - <strong>Mixture</strong> (homogeneous: N₂, O₂, CO₂, etc.)</p>\n                <p>(b) Gold - <strong>Element</strong> (pure substance, one type of atom)</p>\n                <p>(c) Carbon dioxide - <strong>Compound</strong> (C and O chemically combined)</p>\n                <p>(d) Salt solution - <strong>Mixture</strong> (homogeneous: salt dissolved in water)</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Why is air classified as a mixture and not a compound?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>Air is a mixture because:</p>\n                <ul class=\"list-disc list-inside mt-1\">\n                  <li>Components can vary in proportion</li>\n                  <li>Components can be separated physically (e.g., fractional distillation)</li>\n                  <li>No chemical bonds between N₂, O₂, etc.</li>\n                  <li>Components retain their individual properties</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Give two differences between a compound and a mixture.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <table class=\"w-full border-collapse mt-2 text-sm\">\n                  <tbody><tr class=\"bg-gray-100\">\n                    <th class=\"p-2 border text-left\">Compound</th>\n                    <th class=\"p-2 border text-left\">Mixture</th>\n                  </tr>\n                  <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">Fixed composition</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">Variable composition</td></tr>\n                  <tr><td class=\"p-2 border\">Separated by chemical means</td><td class=\"p-2 border\">Separated by physical means</td></tr>\n                </tbody></table>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. Classify: Copper wire, brass, bronze. Explain your answers.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Solution</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p><strong>Copper wire</strong> - Element (pure copper)</p>\n                <p><strong>Brass</strong> - Mixture (copper + zinc, no chemical bonding)</p>\n                <p><strong>Bronze</strong> - Mixture (copper + tin, no chemical bonding)</p>\n                <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">Note: Brass and bronze are alloys - homogeneous mixtures of metals.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <section id=\"section-8\" class=\"mb-8\">\n        <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-emerald-50 to-green-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-emerald-200\">\n          <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-emerald-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways for WAEC/JAMB/NECO</h3>\n          <ul class=\"text-emerald-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n            <li>• <strong>Element:</strong> One type of atom, cannot be broken down further</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Compound:</strong> Fixed ratio, chemical bonds, separated chemically only</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Mixture:</strong> Variable ratio, no chemical bonds, separated physically</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Homogeneous:</strong> Uniform throughout (solutions, alloys)</li>\n            <li>• <strong>Heterogeneous:</strong> Non-uniform, visible components</li>\n            <li>• Know the differences between metals, non-metals, and metalloids</li>\n          </ul>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Complete Topic Button -->\n      <div class=\"mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-gray-200\">\n        <div class=\"flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"text-center sm:text-left\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800\">Ready to Complete?</h3>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">View all sections, then take the quiz to mark this topic as complete.</p>\n          </div>\n          <button id=\"topic-complete-btn\" disabled=\"\" class=\"px-6 py-3 rounded-xl bg-gray-300 text-gray-500 cursor-not-allowed opacity-50 flex items-center gap-2 text-lg font-medium\">\n            <span class=\"mi -lock mr-2\" data-mi=\"lock\">lock</span>\n            <span>Complete (0% viewed)</span>\n          </button>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n  \n\n\n<div data-bidemy=\"quiz\"></div>","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-50 to-green-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n    .content-card {\n      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      backdrop-filter: blur(12px);\n      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95);\n      border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n    }\n    .accordion-content {\n      max-height: 0;\n      overflow: hidden;\n      transition: max-height 0.3s ease-out;\n    }\n    .accordion-content.open {\n      max-height: 2000px;\n    }\n    .step-card { transition: all 0.2s ease; }\n    .step-card:hover { transform: translateX(4px); }\n    #topic-complete-btn { transition: all 0.3s ease; }\n    #topic-complete-btn:not(:disabled):hover { transform: scale(1.02); }"],"quiz":{"topicId":"definition-classification","subject":"chemistry","passingScore":60,"questions":[{"question":"Which of the following is an element?","options":["Water","Air","Iron","Salt"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Iron (Fe) is an element - it consists of only one type of atom."},{"question":"A compound can be separated by:","options":["Filtration","Distillation","Chemical means only","Evaporation"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Compounds require chemical reactions to separate their components."},{"question":"Which is a homogeneous mixture?","options":["Sand and water","Oil and water","Salt solution","Salad"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Salt solution is homogeneous - the salt is evenly dissolved throughout."},{"question":"Water (H₂O) is a compound because:","options":["It is a liquid","Hydrogen and oxygen are in fixed ratio","It contains hydrogen","It is colorless"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Compounds have fixed ratios by mass - water always has 2 H : 1 O."},{"question":"Which property is typical of metals?","options":["Poor conductor","Brittle","Dull appearance","Malleable"],"correct":3,"explanation":"Metals are malleable - they can be hammered into sheets."},{"question":"Air is classified as a mixture because:","options":["It contains oxygen","Components can vary in proportion","It is invisible","It supports life"],"correct":1,"explanation":"Mixtures have variable composition - air composition can change."},{"question":"Brass (copper + zinc) is:","options":["An element","A compound","A homogeneous mixture","A heterogeneous mixture"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Brass is an alloy - a homogeneous mixture of metals."},{"question":"Which shows properties different from its constituents?","options":["Salt solution","Air","Water","Sand and water"],"correct":2,"explanation":"Compounds have different properties from their elements. Water (extinguishes fire) differs from hydrogen (flammable) and oxygen (supports burning)."}]},"tracker":{"topicId":"definition-classification","topicTitle":"Definition & Classification of Matter","subject":"chemistry","sections":["section-1","section-2","section-3","section-4","section-5","section-6","section-7","section-8"],"quizRequired":true},"links":[]}